1
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:33,909
[This drama is fiction.]

2
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:36,036
[Characters, places, events, organization,
and the setting have no connection to reality.]

3
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,438
[Child actors
were filmed under safe conditions.]

4
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:43,709
Counsel for the defendant?

5
00:00:43,709 --> 00:00:47,359
Why don't we settle this and wrap it up here?

6
00:00:49,792 --> 00:00:51,476
We cannot settle.

7
00:00:51,476 --> 00:00:55,586
Your Honor, not all affairs are the same.

8
00:00:55,586 --> 00:00:58,132
An affair is an affair.

9
00:00:58,132 --> 00:01:01,942
Are you claiming there are degrees
of illegality in an affair?

10
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:04,067
No.

11
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:08,287
I'm claiming there is no illegality.

12
00:01:21,668 --> 00:01:27,848
[Case 01: Good Partner]

13
00:01:28,876 --> 00:01:32,993
We will now begin the presentation
of the Power Woman of the Year award.

14
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:37,318
The winner is Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.

15
00:01:40,792 --> 00:01:46,940
She built a law firm with 50 people
in just three years.

16
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,125
Congratulations on your award.

17
00:01:50,125 --> 00:01:54,500
A lawyer who puts skill, principles,
and people first.

18
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,244
Selected as one of today's
most notable female leaders,

19
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:04,917
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.
Please give her a warm round of applause.

20
00:02:11,042 --> 00:02:14,375
Attorney Cha, please introduce yourself.

21
00:02:14,375 --> 00:02:18,553
Hello. I'm the representative attorney
of Korea's only divorce law firm,

22
00:02:18,553 --> 00:02:21,719
Cha Eun Kyung from REBOM Law Firm.

23
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:23,744
Nice to meet you.

24
00:02:27,334 --> 00:02:31,876
REBOM has seen remarkable growth
in just three years.

25
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:36,234
What is the secret to such rapid growth?

26
00:02:37,637 --> 00:02:39,311
Sales skills.

27
00:02:39,311 --> 00:02:41,292
Sales... skills?

28
00:02:41,292 --> 00:02:44,584
Do you mean marketing or promotion?

29
00:02:44,584 --> 00:02:45,875
No.

30
00:02:45,875 --> 00:02:50,160
Sales skills ultimately come from sincerity.

31
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:55,384
There are 36,000 lawyers now,
and 27,000 of them are in Seoul.

32
00:02:55,384 --> 00:03:00,055
The only way to survive this jungle
is not to take on cases,

33
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:02,894
but to provide solutions
for the clients' lives.

34
00:03:02,894 --> 00:03:06,882
The best result is the best sales pitch.

35
00:03:06,882 --> 00:03:13,159
"The best result is the best sales pitch."
That's a great quote.

36
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:15,654
Now I can't help but wonder.

37
00:03:15,654 --> 00:03:18,240
What is REBOM's next goal?

38
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:21,125
REBOM is preparing for an expansion.

39
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:27,250
We plan to reach 30 billion won in sales
and enter the top 30 firms in Korea.

40
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:29,803
We'll be rooting for you.

41
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:43,234
That was this year's Power Woman,
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.

42
00:03:58,899 --> 00:04:00,942
[Central Family Court]

43
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:30,317
[REBOM Law Firm]

44
00:04:37,645 --> 00:04:40,374
Good morning, ma'am.

45
00:04:43,985 --> 00:04:45,681
Hello.

46
00:04:46,999 --> 00:04:50,501
- Good morning.
- Hello.

47
00:04:51,377 --> 00:04:53,792
- Hello.
- Good morning.

48
00:04:53,792 --> 00:04:55,891
The Senior Partner is here.

49
00:04:56,493 --> 00:04:58,835
Selected as Korea's Power Woman.

50
00:04:58,835 --> 00:05:00,786
Congratulations.

51
00:05:04,751 --> 00:05:08,266
Ma'am, how about a team dinner tonight?

52
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,306
A team dinner.

53
00:05:09,306 --> 00:05:14,728
- Team dinner.
- Team dinner.

54
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:18,082
Wait a minute.

55
00:05:18,082 --> 00:05:21,787
Let's have it
when we expand to the eighth floor.

56
00:05:23,167 --> 00:05:25,575
Yes. Shall we? That would be better.

57
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:29,417
To be exact, I'm the one who won the award,
not REBOM, right?

58
00:05:29,417 --> 00:05:32,942
Let's break it up and get back to work.
Thank you.

59
00:05:36,292 --> 00:05:41,407
She's saying we should share the joy
when it's not a personal event

60
00:05:41,407 --> 00:05:44,427
but a celebration for all of us.

61
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:47,639
Yes. Please get back to what you need to do.

62
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:51,109
I told you not to use confetti. Thank you.

63
00:06:01,089 --> 00:06:02,489
What?

64
00:06:05,542 --> 00:06:08,709
Congratulations again, ma'am.

65
00:06:08,709 --> 00:06:11,109
I'll put this over there.

66
00:06:11,876 --> 00:06:14,426
I told them you don't like parties,

67
00:06:14,426 --> 00:06:17,285
but they all insisted on celebrating.

68
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:24,168
Ma'am, we're in Season 2 now.
Will we be okay like this?

69
00:06:24,168 --> 00:06:25,209
Season 2?

70
00:06:25,209 --> 00:06:29,876
We're not a small office anymore.
We're a firm with 50 employees.

71
00:06:29,876 --> 00:06:32,544
So it's Season 2 of REBOM.

72
00:06:32,544 --> 00:06:34,250
But it's an emergency, ma'am.

73
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:40,984
A big firm like this only has two lawyers:
you and me.

74
00:06:41,805 --> 00:06:44,146
I let them go because they deserved it.

75
00:06:44,146 --> 00:06:48,667
They don't care about cases and only talk
about shares. What kind of lawyers are they?

76
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:52,329
<i>Make me a partner.
We need to share profits for the firm to grow.</i>

77
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,001
<i>Should've handled your cases first.</i>

78
00:06:54,001 --> 00:06:56,666
<i>Why talk about shares when you lack basics?</i>

79
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:59,593
<i>You hand our cases to other firms
and take referral fees.</i>

80
00:06:59,593 --> 00:07:02,834
<i>Are you a lawyer or a broker? That's illegal.</i>

81
00:07:02,834 --> 00:07:04,633
<i>So what? Are you going to sue me?</i>

82
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:08,845
<i>Don't come in tomorrow. You did nothing,
so there's nothing to pass on.</i>

83
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,257
[Kim Hyun Min]
[Heo Jin Kyung]

84
00:07:14,417 --> 00:07:17,729
I don't need people
who care about their own interests and shares,

85
00:07:17,729 --> 00:07:21,921
not the clients' interests,
at a firm I built with my own blood and sweat.

86
00:07:22,592 --> 00:07:26,119
I'll train a good associate
and make them a partner.

87
00:07:26,119 --> 00:07:28,885
That's when Season 2 of REBOM really begins.

88
00:07:28,885 --> 00:07:30,283
You said you wouldn't do it.

89
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:33,119
It's not that I won't. It's that I can't.

90
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:37,167
I'm the type who needs time to myself
after work, not more sales work...

91
00:07:37,167 --> 00:07:38,893
Anyway, that's not the point.

92
00:07:38,893 --> 00:07:41,002
Ma'am, please make sure

93
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:45,542
to hire a lawyer who will stay with us
for a long time, and do it quickly.

94
00:07:45,542 --> 00:07:47,949
- I'm counting on you.
- I got it. Back to work.

95
00:07:47,949 --> 00:07:49,349
Got it.

96
00:08:02,367 --> 00:08:06,483
Good lawyers are so hard to find.

97
00:08:14,325 --> 00:08:16,367
[REBOM Law Firm eighth floor expansion plan]

98
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:26,584
Ma'am.

99
00:08:26,584 --> 00:08:31,156
Another firm took our ad spot
by paying double the deposit.

100
00:08:31,156 --> 00:08:32,700
What?

101
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:36,100
We were going to use that spot
to promote the eighth floor.

102
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,054
[Skill is the strategy]

103
00:09:28,941 --> 00:09:31,468
[Problem Solver Kang Hye Seong]

104
00:09:46,183 --> 00:09:48,804
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm's Problem Solver]
[Attorney Kang Hye Seong]

105
00:10:02,173 --> 00:10:06,187
[For Divorce Cases, Kang Hye Seong]

106
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:15,792
Please wait over there, thank you.

107
00:10:15,792 --> 00:10:17,375
Hello.

108
00:10:17,375 --> 00:10:19,709
Village Chief.

109
00:10:19,709 --> 00:10:22,497
Isn't Attorney Kang Hye Seong here yet?

110
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:24,978
She went to court, but she'll be back soon.

111
00:10:24,978 --> 00:10:26,275
Oh, there she is.

112
00:10:26,275 --> 00:10:27,626
Attorney Kang.

113
00:10:27,626 --> 00:10:30,814
Village Chief.
You shouldn't bring so much food every time.

114
00:10:30,814 --> 00:10:33,341
We won the case because of you.

115
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:38,639
How did you turn around a case
we completely lost in the first trial?

116
00:10:39,531 --> 00:10:41,334
[Court]

117
00:10:41,334 --> 00:10:43,309
<i>The defendant's dog barks every night</i>

118
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:45,390
<i>causing the plaintiff chronic headaches,</i>

119
00:10:45,390 --> 00:10:47,538
<i>so the claim for damages was granted.</i>

120
00:10:47,538 --> 00:10:49,481
<i>Since defendant lost the first trial,</i>

121
00:10:49,481 --> 00:10:52,357
<i>it's hard to hold further hearings
without new evidence.</i>

122
00:10:52,357 --> 00:10:55,709
<i>I take it you have no new evidence to present?</i>

123
00:10:55,709 --> 00:10:58,400
<i>Your Honor, I have evidence.</i>

124
00:11:01,042 --> 00:11:03,121
<i>Do you know this dog?</i>

125
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:05,415
<i>- I know Bokdong.
- Does he bark a lot?</i>

126
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,388
<i>- He doesn't.
- Bokdong's a good boy.</i>

127
00:11:07,388 --> 00:11:09,125
<i>- A good boy?
- Yes.</i>

128
00:11:09,125 --> 00:11:13,542
<i>Ma'am, could I take a look
at the security camera footage?</i>

129
00:11:13,542 --> 00:11:14,674
<i>Can I help you?</i>

130
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:16,518
<i>Could I check the dashcam footage?</i>

131
00:11:16,518 --> 00:11:21,584
<i>Based on the neighbors' statements
and the security camera investigation,</i>

132
00:11:21,584 --> 00:11:25,067
<i>the defendant's dog didn't bark for no reason.</i>

133
00:11:25,959 --> 00:11:31,483
<i>He barked instinctively whenever someone tried
to break into the plaintiff's house.</i>

134
00:11:31,483 --> 00:11:37,258
<i>Thanks to the defendant's dog,
the plaintiff was able to prevent a break-in.</i>

135
00:11:38,042 --> 00:11:41,333
<i>A dog's instinctive reaction
to a dangerous situation</i>

136
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:45,029
<i>can't be called illegal noise
beyond what neighbors should bear.</i>

137
00:11:45,029 --> 00:11:47,168
Thank you so much, Attorney Kang.

138
00:11:47,168 --> 00:11:49,959
For letting me live with Bokdong again.

139
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:53,053
I'm so grateful
that I would like to refer a case to you.

140
00:11:53,053 --> 00:11:55,876
Do you handle divorce cases too?

141
00:11:55,876 --> 00:11:59,609
Yes, of course!
Divorce cases are my absolute favorite.

142
00:12:01,412 --> 00:12:03,173
That's good.

143
00:12:05,792 --> 00:12:07,288
Yes.

144
00:12:08,854 --> 00:12:13,209
Attorney Kang, are you working late again?

145
00:12:13,209 --> 00:12:18,007
You're the only lawyer here,
yet you take on every minor case that comes in.

146
00:12:18,007 --> 00:12:20,507
It's not like this firm specializes in them.

147
00:12:20,507 --> 00:12:25,318
How can you handle all these people
and all these different fields alone?

148
00:12:26,755 --> 00:12:28,613
Escape while you can.

149
00:12:30,414 --> 00:12:35,000
But thanks to the boss, these minor... I mean,

150
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,626
I'm getting experience with various cases.

151
00:12:38,626 --> 00:12:39,968
Well,

152
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:42,940
at least you have a divorce consultation
tomorrow, and you like those.

153
00:12:45,435 --> 00:12:48,971
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm]

154
00:12:56,292 --> 00:12:58,487
What is the reason for the divorce?

155
00:12:59,334 --> 00:13:03,073
My wife... had an affair.

156
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:17,315
The evidence is sufficient.

157
00:13:17,315 --> 00:13:19,083
You'll proceed with the divorce, right?

158
00:13:19,083 --> 00:13:21,109
I'm such a fool.

159
00:13:22,542 --> 00:13:27,775
My feelings don't just disappear
even if she cheated.

160
00:13:29,393 --> 00:13:31,501
I loved her so much...

161
00:13:33,685 --> 00:13:35,182
But still,

162
00:13:36,167 --> 00:13:40,067
it was a very difficult decision
for me to get a divorce.

163
00:13:42,417 --> 00:13:44,292
That's wise.

164
00:13:44,292 --> 00:13:48,734
I often see people who just forgive
and move on after going through this.

165
00:13:49,864 --> 00:13:52,456
If she did wrong, you should get a divorce.

166
00:13:56,709 --> 00:13:59,926
Based on this evidence,
you have a 99% chance of winning.

167
00:13:59,926 --> 00:14:01,620
It's clearly an affair.

168
00:14:11,908 --> 00:14:13,815
[Motel Shim]

169
00:14:13,815 --> 00:14:18,984
Is it a 100% chance I'll get divorced?

170
00:14:18,984 --> 00:14:24,518
Not 100%, but about 99%.

171
00:14:25,626 --> 00:14:28,525
Then there's no hope...

172
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,637
Even if it's a 99% losing case,

173
00:14:31,637 --> 00:14:35,966
it's our job to fight for that 1% chance.

174
00:14:35,966 --> 00:14:37,710
Judges are human too.

175
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:41,033
We can't predict a verdict with 100% certainty.

176
00:14:41,033 --> 00:14:47,256
Once you receive the complaint,
I'll look for even a 1% opening to rebut it.

177
00:14:47,256 --> 00:14:51,030
I really don't want to get divorced.

178
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:53,518
This is my second marriage.

179
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:55,759
I can't get divorced twice.

180
00:14:55,759 --> 00:14:59,333
That's why I came to REBOM Law Firm,
the best in the industry.

181
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:02,074
Please help me.

182
00:15:02,074 --> 00:15:07,792
Since your husband wants a divorce,
he'll be sending a complaint soon.

183
00:15:07,792 --> 00:15:11,026
Come back then,
and we'll have another consultation.

184
00:15:12,918 --> 00:15:15,032
What does your asset situation look like?

185
00:15:15,032 --> 00:15:16,712
Don't even get me started.

186
00:15:16,712 --> 00:15:20,083
My father gave my wife a condo
worth 100 million won.

187
00:15:20,083 --> 00:15:23,751
I was going to sell it
and expand the stray dog shelter.

188
00:15:23,751 --> 00:15:25,635
I really want that money back.

189
00:15:25,635 --> 00:15:30,344
It's getting hotter,
and my dogs need to be in a better facility.

190
00:15:30,344 --> 00:15:33,078
So please end the lawsuit quickly.

191
00:15:34,292 --> 00:15:38,663
Sadly, I can't promise a quick divorce
with no property division for her.

192
00:15:38,663 --> 00:15:42,824
A lawyer can't customize a ruling like that.

193
00:15:43,577 --> 00:15:45,805
For property division...

194
00:15:45,805 --> 00:15:48,375
it'll be at least 30 million won.

195
00:15:48,375 --> 00:15:50,116
What?

196
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:55,018
You want me to give 30 million won
to a woman who cheated?

197
00:15:55,018 --> 00:15:56,733
I know it sounds unfair.

198
00:15:56,733 --> 00:16:02,292
What I don't get is why the law gives
property division to the one who cheated.

199
00:16:02,292 --> 00:16:05,330
But we'll offset the division
with the compensation she owes.

200
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:07,718
And try our best to get the condo back.

201
00:16:07,718 --> 00:16:09,367
Okay.

202
00:16:10,584 --> 00:16:15,417
I'm counting on you.
Please make sure I get this divorce.

203
00:16:15,417 --> 00:16:16,560
She's too clingy.

204
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:19,372
With someone like that,
a quick divorce is the answer.

205
00:16:19,372 --> 00:16:21,167
I'll file the complaint now.

206
00:16:21,167 --> 00:16:22,567
Yes.

207
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:25,953
Mom.

208
00:16:25,953 --> 00:16:27,212
Hey.

209
00:16:29,133 --> 00:16:30,546
Good job today.

210
00:16:30,546 --> 00:16:31,935
Aren't you tired?

211
00:16:31,935 --> 00:16:33,532
I'm okay.

212
00:16:45,255 --> 00:16:48,871
You promised to rest on the days
you go to your dad's.

213
00:16:48,871 --> 00:16:50,593
Stop looking at the workbook.

214
00:16:50,593 --> 00:16:54,306
No, it's inefficient to space out in the car.

215
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:58,411
You know, since high school,
you're becoming less and less human.

216
00:16:58,411 --> 00:16:59,873
Guess who I take after.

217
00:16:59,873 --> 00:17:03,250
Mom, I'm switching to Ji Yoon's math academy.

218
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:06,292
Why? Don't you like the one you go to now?

219
00:17:06,292 --> 00:17:08,083
I'll look for a new place for you.

220
00:17:08,083 --> 00:17:11,078
How many times have you said that?
I'll handle it myself.

221
00:17:11,078 --> 00:17:14,482
Civil Code Article 4:
A person reaches adulthood at the age of 19.

222
00:17:14,482 --> 00:17:16,714
I'll be an adult in three years.

223
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:35,296
Welcome, Jae Hee.

224
00:17:40,762 --> 00:17:42,162
Jae Hee.

225
00:17:42,959 --> 00:17:44,745
- I'll go in first.
- Okay.

226
00:17:44,745 --> 00:17:46,619
Drive safely, Mom.

227
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:50,805
These are frozen dumplings.
Jae Hee really likes them.

228
00:17:50,805 --> 00:17:52,541
Keep them home for her.

229
00:17:55,692 --> 00:17:57,384
Could you do that, please?

230
00:17:58,661 --> 00:18:00,534
Jae Hee eats dumplings?

231
00:18:00,534 --> 00:18:02,083
She used to not like them.

232
00:18:02,083 --> 00:18:05,620
She didn't like store-bought ones.
She liked homemade ones.

233
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:08,093
You made dumplings yourself?

234
00:18:08,093 --> 00:18:11,750
No, when would I have time for that?
Ji Yoon's mom did.

235
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:13,850
Ta-da!

236
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:16,096
- Thank you.
- Eat up.

237
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:21,649
Jae Hee wants to switch math academies.

238
00:18:21,649 --> 00:18:23,046
I'll change it and let you know.

239
00:18:23,046 --> 00:18:25,281
Thanks. Go on.

240
00:18:25,281 --> 00:18:26,626
Yeah.

241
00:18:26,626 --> 00:18:29,292
- I'll win for sure.
- I'll definitely win.

242
00:18:29,292 --> 00:18:32,250
Jae Hee, want Dad to roast one?
I'm a marshmallow expert.

243
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:35,000
You always burn them, Dad.

244
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,626
Honey, I'll do it.

245
00:18:36,626 --> 00:18:40,292
- I'm good at this.
- Just wait.

246
00:18:40,292 --> 00:18:42,751
- I won.
- No, you didn't.

247
00:18:42,751 --> 00:18:44,458
- I'm really good at this.
- No.

248
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:46,815
Let's see.

249
00:18:55,196 --> 00:18:56,827
[Manage My Cases]

250
00:18:56,827 --> 00:18:57,877
[Ongoing Case]

251
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:02,083
[Search]

252
00:19:03,927 --> 00:19:05,329
[Counsel for Defendant]

253
00:19:07,105 --> 00:19:09,105
[REBOM Attorneys: Cha Eun Kyung, Jeon Eun Ho]

254
00:19:29,824 --> 00:19:32,556
Wow, it's the Han River.

255
00:19:43,667 --> 00:19:46,728
I'll only attend the first hearing
for today's trial.

256
00:19:46,728 --> 00:19:50,280
Per contract,
you will handle it from the second hearing.

257
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,758
Yes, ma'am.

258
00:19:51,758 --> 00:19:53,751
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

259
00:19:53,751 --> 00:19:56,356
Actually, I'm a bit worried lately.

260
00:19:56,356 --> 00:19:59,957
What senior partner goes to court this often?

261
00:19:59,957 --> 00:20:02,792
Between trials, sales,
consultations, and TV work...

262
00:20:02,792 --> 00:20:07,493
I'm so anxious that you might get burned out.

263
00:20:07,493 --> 00:20:08,904
So if you ask me,

264
00:20:08,904 --> 00:20:13,375
it would be great to hire a new lawyer soon.
What do you think?

265
00:20:13,375 --> 00:20:15,542
You're worried about me, right?

266
00:20:15,542 --> 00:20:16,876
Of course. Definitely.

267
00:20:16,876 --> 00:20:21,619
And actually, I'm a bit worried about myself.
I need my own time after work.

268
00:20:21,619 --> 00:20:26,395
But since I don't have that lately,
I wonder if this is what they call overwork.

269
00:20:26,395 --> 00:20:29,334
What do you think about that?

270
00:20:29,334 --> 00:20:34,358
Attorney Jeon, do you smile like that
while attacking your opponent in court?

271
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,943
You're good at this.

272
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:37,584
Thank you.

273
00:20:37,584 --> 00:20:40,217
We're in the middle of hiring, so don't worry.

274
00:20:40,217 --> 00:20:41,535
Yes, ma'am.

275
00:21:05,125 --> 00:21:06,417
Seo Ji Hoon?

276
00:21:06,417 --> 00:21:08,192
Yes, Attorney.

277
00:21:09,947 --> 00:21:12,709
Was the traffic heavy?

278
00:21:12,709 --> 00:21:14,626
The trial is still five minutes away.

279
00:21:14,626 --> 00:21:18,292
Yes, but I'm a bit nervous.

280
00:21:18,292 --> 00:21:21,404
The other side is the famous
Cha Eun Kyung's firm.

281
00:21:21,404 --> 00:21:23,083
Will we be okay?

282
00:21:23,083 --> 00:21:25,452
The head of the firm rarely appears in person.

283
00:21:25,452 --> 00:21:28,417
And why be anxious? Their fault is clear.

284
00:21:28,417 --> 00:21:31,709
You'll be relieved once you see
how I present the case.

285
00:21:31,709 --> 00:21:33,203
Let's go in.

286
00:21:45,667 --> 00:21:47,448
<i>It's Cha Eun Kyung.</i>

287
00:22:05,755 --> 00:22:07,405
Let's go too.

288
00:22:10,334 --> 00:22:13,959
Attorney Kang Hye Seong
of CHUNJEONG Law Firm is present.

289
00:22:13,959 --> 00:22:17,525
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung
of REBOM Law Firm is present.

290
00:22:23,334 --> 00:22:26,927
Your Honor, he's the one who cheated first.

291
00:22:26,927 --> 00:22:29,591
He's doing this to pin everything on me.

292
00:22:35,626 --> 00:22:37,688
What are you talking about?

293
00:22:37,688 --> 00:22:40,365
The defendant cheated, not the plaintiff.

294
00:22:40,365 --> 00:22:43,115
Your Honor, please show the evidence.

295
00:22:45,329 --> 00:22:48,031
[Is there anyone who can meet
around 9:00 PM tonight?]

296
00:22:48,031 --> 00:22:49,499
[Let's meet at Hotel Argen in Seoul]

297
00:22:49,499 --> 00:22:51,037
[Whoever gets there first, message me]

298
00:23:08,751 --> 00:23:12,976
I won't agree to a divorce.
Please protect my family, Your Honor.

299
00:23:12,976 --> 00:23:16,501
I really, really didn't sleep with anyone.

300
00:23:17,876 --> 00:23:19,421
You went to the motel...

301
00:23:21,016 --> 00:23:24,250
You went to the motel,
but you didn't sleep with anyone?

302
00:23:24,250 --> 00:23:27,042
Hey, you know I really
didn't sleep with anyone!

303
00:23:27,042 --> 00:23:28,781
Order in the court.

304
00:23:30,709 --> 00:23:35,895
You say there was no sex,
despite all this evidence of seeking partners?

305
00:23:35,895 --> 00:23:38,323
This is a court of law.

306
00:23:39,177 --> 00:23:41,720
The plaintiff's counsel traveled a long way,

307
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:44,755
so she may have missed
our evidence from this morning.

308
00:23:44,755 --> 00:23:46,570
Could you please display it?

309
00:24:06,661 --> 00:24:08,751
<i>They both cheated?</i>

310
00:24:13,959 --> 00:24:17,459
The plaintiff was the one who cheated first.

311
00:24:17,459 --> 00:24:22,411
And the defendant's affair was
due to the plaintiff's threats and coercion.

312
00:24:22,411 --> 00:24:24,593
Threats and coercion?

313
00:24:24,593 --> 00:24:29,029
Who in their right mind would threaten
their spouse into having an affair?

314
00:24:29,029 --> 00:24:31,145
He's sitting right next to you.

315
00:24:31,145 --> 00:24:33,424
I guess you didn't know, Counselor.

316
00:24:37,334 --> 00:24:40,105
Your false claims are excessive.
Can you prove them?

317
00:24:40,105 --> 00:24:43,006
Yes. Digital forensics is currently underway.

318
00:24:44,167 --> 00:24:45,275
Your Honor.

319
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:47,687
Please record that the defendant's counsel

320
00:24:47,687 --> 00:24:50,709
just admitted to the defendant's infidelity.

321
00:24:50,709 --> 00:24:54,485
Go ahead. We admit to the "act" of infidelity.

322
00:24:54,485 --> 00:24:57,542
<i>She's admitting it? In court?</i>

323
00:24:57,542 --> 00:24:59,363
We admit the act itself.

324
00:24:59,363 --> 00:25:03,626
However,
that act does not make her the party at fault.

325
00:25:03,626 --> 00:25:07,650
If you're so desperate to get it on the record,
by all means.

326
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:23,530
Seo Ji Hoon.

327
00:25:27,027 --> 00:25:30,817
Seo Ji Hoon, you should have told me
that you also had an affair.

328
00:25:31,752 --> 00:25:33,716
I'm sorry.

329
00:25:33,716 --> 00:25:37,542
I only suggested we both admit it
and divorce by mutual agreement.

330
00:25:37,542 --> 00:25:42,835
But she refused to divorce me,
so I had no choice but to file a lawsuit.

331
00:25:42,835 --> 00:25:45,193
I didn't know she had evidence.

332
00:25:46,083 --> 00:25:51,224
What about the claim that you
threatened her to have sex with other men?

333
00:25:51,224 --> 00:25:53,456
That's absolutely not true. Never.

334
00:25:53,456 --> 00:25:56,054
Think about it. Why would I threaten her?

335
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:59,883
She's lying to cover her own fault
because she doesn't want a divorce.

336
00:25:59,883 --> 00:26:01,277
I see.

337
00:26:01,277 --> 00:26:02,949
Since both are at fault,

338
00:26:02,949 --> 00:26:06,268
I'll argue the marriage is broken
to get a divorce ruling.

339
00:26:06,959 --> 00:26:09,167
You worked so hard today.

340
00:26:09,167 --> 00:26:11,167
- Great job.
- Yes, we'll be in touch.

341
00:26:11,167 --> 00:26:13,924
- Yes, thank you.
- Take care.

342
00:26:15,518 --> 00:26:16,918
- Thanks.
- Good job.

343
00:26:16,918 --> 00:26:18,578
Secretary Kim is outside.

344
00:26:18,578 --> 00:26:20,301
Okay.

345
00:26:20,301 --> 00:26:21,867
Counselor!

346
00:26:23,892 --> 00:26:28,211
Counselor, so you're saying the plaintiff
told the defendant to have an affair,

347
00:26:28,211 --> 00:26:31,553
and since she did as told,
she's not at fault? Is that it?

348
00:26:31,553 --> 00:26:33,383
Exactly.

349
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:35,141
If a client makes a ridiculous claim,

350
00:26:35,141 --> 00:26:38,296
isn't it a lawyer's job to refine it
and present it to court?

351
00:26:38,296 --> 00:26:40,037
And when both sides are at fault,

352
00:26:40,037 --> 00:26:44,677
99% of lawyers propose a settlement
instead of pushing an unreasonable claim.

353
00:26:44,677 --> 00:26:51,276
If that's all a lawyer does,
an AI could do it. Why did you even show up?

354
00:26:52,020 --> 00:26:55,733
You said it's an absurd claim.
By whose standards?

355
00:26:57,667 --> 00:27:00,864
This isn't your first divorce case, is it?

356
00:27:00,864 --> 00:27:02,538
Well, not exactly my first...

357
00:27:02,538 --> 00:27:07,536
Divorce cases are a 1% fight, not a 99% one.

358
00:27:07,536 --> 00:27:13,342
And there's no such thing as absurd
in this world.

359
00:27:13,342 --> 00:27:15,371
That's normal for a rookie.

360
00:27:15,371 --> 00:27:18,596
Try to broaden your perspective.

361
00:27:22,392 --> 00:27:24,977
So, since we have different positions,

362
00:27:24,977 --> 00:27:29,000
I suppose she's saying we should
both do our best for our clients.

363
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,567
We'll see you at the next hearing, Counselor.

364
00:27:38,743 --> 00:27:42,063
Some lawyer she is.

365
00:27:46,756 --> 00:27:48,168
Please check here.

366
00:27:48,168 --> 00:27:50,125
Okay.

367
00:27:50,125 --> 00:27:52,745
- You're back, Attorney.
- Yes.

368
00:27:55,008 --> 00:27:56,607
Just a moment.

369
00:27:58,584 --> 00:28:00,169
Yes.

370
00:28:04,334 --> 00:28:06,626
Attorney, how was it?

371
00:28:06,626 --> 00:28:09,091
It was a divorce trial in Seoul,
which you love,

372
00:28:09,091 --> 00:28:13,496
and you even met a top-tier divorce lawyer.

373
00:28:13,496 --> 00:28:16,177
It was a mess on a whole other level.

374
00:28:16,177 --> 00:28:20,292
I thought he was the victim,
but they both cheated.

375
00:28:20,292 --> 00:28:23,834
No way. He looked so innocent.

376
00:28:23,834 --> 00:28:25,384
Right?

377
00:28:25,384 --> 00:28:28,005
It was bad enough my client
stabbed me in the back,

378
00:28:28,005 --> 00:28:32,375
but Attorney Cha Eun Kyung lied through
her teeth rather than offer a settlement.

379
00:28:32,375 --> 00:28:34,529
I'm so disappointed.

380
00:28:34,529 --> 00:28:35,700
Seriously.

381
00:28:35,700 --> 00:28:38,381
Hey, Kang. Come to my office right now!

382
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,166
Kang, wrap that case up quickly.

383
00:28:50,166 --> 00:28:53,042
A divorce rookie like you
can never beat Cha Eun Kyung.

384
00:28:53,042 --> 00:28:57,394
Sir, I don't think fame and talent
are proportional.

385
00:28:57,394 --> 00:29:00,460
I plan to do my best in this case too.

386
00:29:01,256 --> 00:29:04,079
Don't be stupid. It's a trial in Seoul.

387
00:29:04,079 --> 00:29:08,139
If it drags on,
gas will cost more than the retainer fee.

388
00:29:08,139 --> 00:29:10,189
It's not cost-effective!

389
00:29:10,189 --> 00:29:11,664
Just settle.

390
00:29:12,814 --> 00:29:16,473
Sir, this is the first divorce case
we have had in a year.

391
00:29:16,473 --> 00:29:19,167
Did you forget your promise
when I joined the firm?

392
00:29:19,167 --> 00:29:22,708
[4 years ago]
<i>I want to become a divorce specialist.</i>

393
00:29:22,708 --> 00:29:25,908
<i>- Does CHUNJEONG get many divorce cases?
- Of course.</i>

394
00:29:25,908 --> 00:29:27,540
<i>Tons of them.</i>

395
00:29:28,517 --> 00:29:30,589
How long ago was that?

396
00:29:30,589 --> 00:29:32,329
Divorce doesn't make money.

397
00:29:32,329 --> 00:29:33,792
You may leave.

398
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:41,900
Yes.

399
00:29:44,375 --> 00:29:47,247
Another stack coming in.

400
00:29:49,831 --> 00:29:52,622
[Jeon Eun Ho]
You can't be serious.

401
00:29:52,622 --> 00:29:53,959
It must be tough.

402
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:57,459
The two of you are handling
over 100 cases right now.

403
00:29:57,459 --> 00:30:00,740
You should just become a partner
and help her out, Attorney Jeon.

404
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:04,845
You know better than anyone why
she wants to grow the firm.

405
00:30:04,845 --> 00:30:06,262
- Manager Shim.
- Yes?

406
00:30:06,262 --> 00:30:09,106
Do you know what I'm most confident in?

407
00:30:09,106 --> 00:30:10,600
Rocket divorces?

408
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:12,500
You're great at finishing cases fast.

409
00:30:12,500 --> 00:30:14,209
Work-life balance?

410
00:30:14,209 --> 00:30:18,500
I heard you were a legend at a major law firm
for always leaving right on time.

411
00:30:18,500 --> 00:30:20,860
Rocket divorces, work-life balance...

412
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:22,384
It's not easy anymore.

413
00:30:22,384 --> 00:30:27,209
My specialty is metacognition.
In other words, knowing my place.

414
00:30:27,209 --> 00:30:32,151
I'm just not partner material at all.

415
00:30:33,542 --> 00:30:36,667
<i>Don't worry. We're in the middle of hiring.</i>

416
00:30:36,667 --> 00:30:39,500
Anyway, enjoy your meal.

417
00:30:39,500 --> 00:30:41,751
Yes, enjoy your meal.

418
00:30:41,751 --> 00:30:44,310
- Ma'am, are you heading out to eat?
- Yeah.

419
00:30:50,625 --> 00:30:52,547
<i>If a client makes a ridiculous claim,</i>

420
00:30:52,547 --> 00:30:56,083
<i>isn't it a lawyer's job to refine it
and present it to court?</i>

421
00:30:56,083 --> 00:30:59,494
She's got guts for a rookie.

422
00:30:59,494 --> 00:31:00,775
Bingo.

423
00:31:00,775 --> 00:31:04,167
That was Attorney Kang Hye Seong, right?
From earlier?

424
00:31:04,167 --> 00:31:06,500
No. Just eat.

425
00:31:06,500 --> 00:31:08,144
I thought she was cool.

426
00:31:08,144 --> 00:31:11,501
It was obvious
her client stabbed her in the back,

427
00:31:11,501 --> 00:31:14,664
but she kept cool so the judge wouldn't notice.

428
00:31:15,814 --> 00:31:20,764
She was like, "Your false claims are excessive.
Can you prove them?"

429
00:31:20,764 --> 00:31:23,127
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

430
00:31:23,127 --> 00:31:25,931
I can't stand people with such narrow views.

431
00:31:29,049 --> 00:31:31,626
I have hired a new lawyer to start soon.

432
00:31:31,626 --> 00:31:34,792
Is a new lawyer finally coming?

433
00:31:34,792 --> 00:31:40,167
But did you find someone who meets
your standards that quickly?

434
00:31:40,167 --> 00:31:42,244
- My standards?
- Yes.

435
00:31:42,244 --> 00:31:45,000
At least five years' experience,
serious about divorce,

436
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,584
- Right.
- and good at handling cases.

437
00:31:47,584 --> 00:31:52,271
Those three are actually
quite strict standards.

438
00:31:52,271 --> 00:31:56,284
It's just that not many lawyers
actually like divorce cases.

439
00:31:56,284 --> 00:32:01,477
And by their fifth year,
they're more interested in sales than cases.

440
00:32:01,477 --> 00:32:04,457
I found one.
So hang in there for a few more days.

441
00:32:04,457 --> 00:32:08,209
And ma'am, about losing that billboard spot...

442
00:32:08,209 --> 00:32:10,743
Just think of it as warding off bad luck.

443
00:32:10,743 --> 00:32:13,083
Once we expand to the eighth floor and grow,

444
00:32:13,083 --> 00:32:14,850
and once the new lawyer arrives,

445
00:32:14,850 --> 00:32:16,935
everything will go smoothly for us.

446
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:19,335
It doesn't bother me.

447
00:32:19,335 --> 00:32:21,162
I'll focus on the eighth-floor expansion.

448
00:32:21,162 --> 00:32:22,562
Yes, ma'am.

449
00:32:25,125 --> 00:32:28,334
Ma'am, I'll head out first for my next trial.

450
00:32:28,334 --> 00:32:29,867
- Go on.
- Thanks for the meal.

451
00:32:29,867 --> 00:32:32,142
- Good luck.
- Yes, ma'am.

452
00:32:33,459 --> 00:32:35,390
Thank you for coming.

453
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:48,375
Isn't that Park Tae Su from By the Law?

454
00:32:48,375 --> 00:32:49,467
It is.

455
00:32:49,467 --> 00:32:51,928
Aren't he and Cha Eun Kyung
the top two in divorce?

456
00:32:51,928 --> 00:32:54,876
Judging by the view counts,
he'll be number one soon.

457
00:32:54,876 --> 00:32:57,375
Already? How many views does he have?

458
00:32:57,375 --> 00:32:59,412
It's around 200,000.

459
00:32:59,412 --> 00:33:01,603
200,000?

460
00:33:04,084 --> 00:33:05,988
Park Tae Su.

461
00:33:07,307 --> 00:33:11,200
[Maximum Divorce Compensation]
[People to Avoid]

462
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:13,400
Is he even a lawyer?

463
00:33:13,400 --> 00:33:15,792
[Park Tae Su Answers Your Questions]

464
00:33:15,792 --> 00:33:18,564
What is the world coming to?

465
00:33:24,102 --> 00:33:25,128
Yes.

466
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:27,110
<i>Ma'am, we're in trouble.</i>

467
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:29,334
Someone else leased the eighth floor.

468
00:33:29,334 --> 00:33:31,918
What do you mean? We have a contract.

469
00:33:31,918 --> 00:33:34,864
They paid the penalty and offered
double the rent for it.

470
00:33:34,864 --> 00:33:36,638
Double again?

471
00:33:37,626 --> 00:33:40,325
Who would do such a thing?

472
00:33:40,325 --> 00:33:42,212
Attorney Park Tae Su did.

473
00:33:47,417 --> 00:33:51,134
If you see Attorney Park Tae Su,
let me know immediately.

474
00:33:51,134 --> 00:33:53,329
I need to see him right now.

475
00:33:58,280 --> 00:34:00,620
[Cool-headed Negotiations, Meticulous Lawsuits]

476
00:34:18,083 --> 00:34:19,682
Seaweed soup?

477
00:34:20,626 --> 00:34:22,948
You remember? It's your mom's birthday.

478
00:34:24,042 --> 00:34:28,567
Dad, did you forget who's responsible
for us living like this?

479
00:34:29,334 --> 00:34:32,010
Haven't seen her in ages. She's not my mom.

480
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:36,650
Still, she's your mother.

481
00:34:47,929 --> 00:34:51,495
<i>No. She's not a mother. She's a perpetrator.</i>

482
00:35:00,584 --> 00:35:02,193
<i>Wrap that case up quickly.</i>

483
00:35:02,193 --> 00:35:06,122
<i>A divorce rookie like you
can never beat Cha Eun Kyung.</i>

484
00:35:06,122 --> 00:35:07,879
<i>That's normal for a rookie.</i>

485
00:35:07,879 --> 00:35:11,456
<i>Try to broaden your perspective.</i>

486
00:35:13,500 --> 00:35:15,900
I'm going to win this case.

487
00:35:31,171 --> 00:35:33,181
[5,000+ Cases: Cha's Argument Skills]

488
00:35:33,181 --> 00:35:35,626
5,000 cases?

489
00:35:35,626 --> 00:35:37,692
Is she that good?

490
00:35:39,083 --> 00:35:43,042
<i>Today, we have Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.
Hello, Attorney Cha.</i>

491
00:35:43,042 --> 00:35:44,754
<i>Hello.</i>

492
00:35:44,754 --> 00:35:49,557
<i>Attorney, I saw a case where a man lied
about his mistress being his sister</i>

493
00:35:49,557 --> 00:35:53,042
<i>and lived with her and his wife
in the same house.</i>

494
00:35:53,042 --> 00:35:56,755
- That's insane.
<i>- Do people like that really exist?</i>

495
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,609
<i>Reality always goes beyond any drama.</i>

496
00:36:00,755 --> 00:36:03,375
What's with that nonchalant expression?

497
00:36:03,375 --> 00:36:07,643
<i>Then do you have your own litigation tips?</i>

498
00:36:07,643 --> 00:36:11,627
<i>Minimize emotions and take
the opponent's key keywords,</i>

499
00:36:11,627 --> 00:36:14,631
<i>then refute them head-on
to highlight the core issues.</i>

500
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:18,167
<i>For example,
if the opponent claims "verbal abuse,"</i>

501
00:36:18,167 --> 00:36:21,305
<i>say, "It was an 'argument'" instead.</i>

502
00:36:21,305 --> 00:36:25,352
<i>Keywords are grounds for fault,
so they stick in the judge's mind.</i>

503
00:36:25,352 --> 00:36:27,337
Keyword refutation.

504
00:36:28,797 --> 00:36:30,751
[Keyword Refutation]

505
00:36:30,751 --> 00:36:32,942
- Yes, thank you.
- Thank you.

506
00:36:39,250 --> 00:36:41,000
- Attorney,
- Yes?

507
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:44,307
Will this be enough to stop the divorce?

508
00:36:44,307 --> 00:36:46,834
Yes, this makes it worth a shot.

509
00:36:46,834 --> 00:36:47,959
Okay.

510
00:36:47,959 --> 00:36:49,243
- Let's go.
- Okay.

511
00:36:55,542 --> 00:36:58,677
Thank you, Attorney. I'll be in touch.

512
00:36:58,677 --> 00:37:00,321
Thank you.

513
00:37:01,292 --> 00:37:03,567
- I'll show you out.
- Sure.

514
00:37:10,375 --> 00:37:11,579
Yes.

515
00:37:12,959 --> 00:37:14,899
Ma'am, what should we do?

516
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:19,446
Attorney Jeon's morning trial ran long,
so he's not back in the office yet.

517
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:21,211
Is that so?

518
00:37:21,211 --> 00:37:24,944
- Then I'll go to Park Na Yeon's trial.
- Yes, ma'am.

519
00:37:33,100 --> 00:37:35,399
[TAESU Law Firm]

520
00:37:42,411 --> 00:37:46,723
The plaintiff told the defendant to go
have sex with a new partner

521
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:49,789
and constantly pressured her
to have relations with others.

522
00:37:49,789 --> 00:37:55,147
His only reason was that their marriage
needed a "refresh."

523
00:37:56,125 --> 00:37:59,692
That claim again? This is ridiculous.

524
00:38:01,459 --> 00:38:06,925
The defendant actually suggested group sex
with three or four people.

525
00:38:06,925 --> 00:38:11,385
Evidence of the defendant recruiting
group sex members has been submitted.

526
00:38:12,125 --> 00:38:13,751
Counsel for the defendant?

527
00:38:13,751 --> 00:38:16,942
Why don't we settle this and wrap it up here?

528
00:38:18,811 --> 00:38:20,509
We cannot settle.

529
00:38:20,509 --> 00:38:24,877
Your Honor, not all affairs are the same.

530
00:38:24,877 --> 00:38:28,099
<i>Did a lawyer just make that claim?</i>

531
00:38:28,825 --> 00:38:31,595
An affair is an affair.

532
00:38:31,595 --> 00:38:35,400
Are you claiming there are degrees
of illegality in an affair?

533
00:38:36,292 --> 00:38:37,834
No.

534
00:38:37,834 --> 00:38:41,067
I'm claiming there is no illegality.

535
00:38:44,165 --> 00:38:48,237
If you're going to make such
a ridiculous claim, provide some evidence.

536
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:53,083
It's an open marriage agreement.

537
00:38:53,083 --> 00:38:56,213
<i>What's this? Open marriage?</i>

538
00:38:59,035 --> 00:39:01,310
[Open Marriage Agreement]

539
00:39:01,310 --> 00:39:03,199
An open marriage agreement,

540
00:39:03,199 --> 00:39:08,252
meaning a free sex or sexual freedom agreement.

541
00:39:16,789 --> 00:39:20,601
The plaintiff, Seo Ji Hoon,
committed adultery "before" the agreement,

542
00:39:20,601 --> 00:39:24,585
while defendant Park Na Yeon only dated
other men "after" it.

543
00:39:24,585 --> 00:39:27,000
Only the plaintiff is at fault.

544
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:29,193
Please dismiss the divorce petition.

545
00:39:30,417 --> 00:39:32,972
Your Honor, the agreement never says

546
00:39:32,972 --> 00:39:38,179
the plaintiff threatened
or coerced her to meet other men.

547
00:39:41,334 --> 00:39:44,417
Your Honor.

548
00:39:44,417 --> 00:39:49,650
I just "happened" to stray,
but she cheated on purpose.

549
00:39:51,334 --> 00:39:52,615
It's okay.

550
00:39:52,615 --> 00:39:57,932
I mean, what man wouldn't fall
for a woman's seduction?

551
00:39:59,954 --> 00:40:03,754
So, the plaintiff's infidelity
was "accidental,"

552
00:40:03,754 --> 00:40:05,650
while hers was "intentional."

553
00:40:05,650 --> 00:40:07,120
Is that your argument?

554
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:09,394
Yes, exactly.

555
00:40:10,083 --> 00:40:13,209
You have quite the legal mind.

556
00:40:13,209 --> 00:40:16,686
You hardly even need a lawyer.

557
00:40:32,256 --> 00:40:38,318
Interpreting "not interfering" as
permission to date other people...

558
00:40:40,709 --> 00:40:43,942
is a subjective interpretation
by defense counsel.

559
00:40:44,723 --> 00:40:49,212
The term "private life" is right there.
How is that subjective?

560
00:40:49,212 --> 00:40:51,765
It's a standard interpretation.

561
00:40:51,765 --> 00:40:55,584
<i>Minimize emotions and take the opponent's
key keywords</i>

562
00:40:55,584 --> 00:40:59,183
<i>then refute them head-on
to highlight the core issues.</i>

563
00:40:59,881 --> 00:41:03,123
Are "private life" and "sex life"
the same thing?

564
00:41:04,970 --> 00:41:07,593
<i>Back in the game. Way to go, girl.</i>

565
00:41:08,521 --> 00:41:10,697
<i>I guess she's not a rookie.</i>

566
00:41:12,254 --> 00:41:16,417
Private life or sex life, what does it matter?

567
00:41:16,417 --> 00:41:22,959
Courts have already ruled that infidelity
doesn't require sex. Surely you know?

568
00:41:22,959 --> 00:41:28,276
That's not even the point.
Let's focus on the actual issue.

569
00:41:38,408 --> 00:41:39,988
Why be like this?

570
00:41:39,988 --> 00:41:42,610
Why on earth would you lie to your own lawyer?

571
00:41:42,610 --> 00:41:44,459
An open marriage?

572
00:41:44,459 --> 00:41:49,806
Actually, it's my first marriage,
but my wife's second.

573
00:41:49,806 --> 00:41:53,653
She said she tried it once
and realized marriage wasn't for her.

574
00:41:53,653 --> 00:41:57,626
She said if she married again,
she wanted to freely sleep with others.

575
00:41:57,626 --> 00:41:59,559
And I was okay with it.

576
00:41:59,559 --> 00:42:03,083
You might think I'm crazy, but at the time,

577
00:42:03,083 --> 00:42:06,168
I wanted to marry her so badly
that I would do anything.

578
00:42:07,334 --> 00:42:10,194
I don't have proof,

579
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:12,626
but my wife was definitely the first to cheat.

580
00:42:12,626 --> 00:42:14,363
So out of spite, I...

581
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:18,832
But now she's pinning it all on me.

582
00:42:22,515 --> 00:42:23,745
<i>See?</i>

583
00:42:23,745 --> 00:42:27,375
<i>You're not satisfied with just me either,
are you?</i>

584
00:42:27,375 --> 00:42:28,817
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

585
00:42:29,542 --> 00:42:34,305
<i>I only did it because you kept
seeing other men. I was just angry.</i>

586
00:42:34,305 --> 00:42:36,887
<i>It didn't mean anything.</i>

587
00:42:36,887 --> 00:42:40,900
<i>Manager Park
from the pet shop kept hitting on me.</i>

588
00:42:41,959 --> 00:42:43,584
<i>No.</i>

589
00:42:43,584 --> 00:42:45,292
<i>Actually, this is better.</i>

590
00:42:45,292 --> 00:42:51,083
<i>Since it's come to this,
let's just sign a formal agreement.</i>

591
00:42:51,083 --> 00:42:53,209
<i>- Here.
- Honey, I'm sorry. Okay?</i>

592
00:42:53,209 --> 00:42:54,500
<i>I'll just...</i>

593
00:42:54,500 --> 00:42:57,762
<i>I have already signed it.
You just need to sign here.</i>

594
00:42:57,762 --> 00:42:59,704
<i>Right here.</i>

595
00:42:59,704 --> 00:43:01,409
<i>Seo Ji Hoon.</i>

596
00:43:20,083 --> 00:43:22,151
I need to take a call.

597
00:43:23,544 --> 00:43:24,802
Understood.

598
00:43:24,802 --> 00:43:29,051
I'm your attorney, so I'll trust you
and defend you until the end.

599
00:43:30,083 --> 00:43:31,567
Thank you.

600
00:43:38,934 --> 00:43:44,274
<i>The AL C&T wife you saw this morning
signed with TAESU Law Firm.</i>

601
00:43:44,871 --> 00:43:47,315
A case worth tens of billions of won...

602
00:43:47,315 --> 00:43:50,415
I can't believe
she hired that attention-seeker.

603
00:43:56,250 --> 00:43:58,168
[Park Tae Su]
But...

604
00:43:58,168 --> 00:44:01,709
Why is TAESU Law Firm's retainer so low?

605
00:44:01,709 --> 00:44:04,459
It's much cheaper than REBOM's.

606
00:44:04,459 --> 00:44:07,250
Instead, the success fee is double.

607
00:44:07,250 --> 00:44:11,489
We save clients' money where we can
and make the other party pay.

608
00:44:11,489 --> 00:44:13,125
That's what real lawyers do.

609
00:44:13,125 --> 00:44:17,859
Then can I really get 50% of the assets?

610
00:44:19,896 --> 00:44:22,580
I don't set such limits.

611
00:44:22,580 --> 00:44:24,980
I'll get you as much as I can.

612
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:53,417
I'm counting on you, Attorney Park.

613
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:14,214
Wow, you were right. This is the best location.

614
00:45:14,214 --> 00:45:19,167
Most clients today said they stopped by
after visiting REBOM.

615
00:45:19,167 --> 00:45:23,140
I told you. It's the perfect spot.

616
00:45:23,140 --> 00:45:26,834
Across from the court, above Cha Eun Kyung.

617
00:45:26,834 --> 00:45:31,417
If we charge half of REBOM's price,
all their cases will come to us.

618
00:45:31,417 --> 00:45:35,209
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung called earlier.

619
00:45:35,209 --> 00:45:36,959
She wants to see you.

620
00:45:36,959 --> 00:45:38,182
Me?

621
00:45:39,918 --> 00:45:42,948
Tell her I'm out. Forever.

622
00:45:44,988 --> 00:45:48,209
[Consultation Lounge]

623
00:45:48,209 --> 00:45:53,362
Looking at today's trial,
I think I was completely played.

624
00:45:53,362 --> 00:45:55,276
It was all a trap.

625
00:46:00,459 --> 00:46:03,959
<i>- How could you do this to me?
- Damn it, you're so annoying.</i>

626
00:46:03,959 --> 00:46:07,334
<i>How can someone be with only one person
for their whole life?</i>

627
00:46:07,334 --> 00:46:10,234
<i>You don't excite me anymore.</i>

628
00:46:11,636 --> 00:46:16,709
<i>Since it's come to this,
let's just enjoy ourselves.</i>

629
00:46:16,709 --> 00:46:17,879
<i>Okay?</i>

630
00:46:17,879 --> 00:46:19,874
<i>Life is short.</i>

631
00:46:22,191 --> 00:46:26,609
<i>Sign this and we stay together.
If not, we get a divorce.</i>

632
00:46:28,500 --> 00:46:30,318
<i>Think carefully.</i>

633
00:46:31,334 --> 00:46:33,626
<i>Do you want to be a woman who divorced twice?</i>

634
00:46:33,626 --> 00:46:35,817
<i>Who would want you then?</i>

635
00:46:49,250 --> 00:46:51,400
<i>Good girl.</i>

636
00:47:02,584 --> 00:47:05,667
[Married woman in 30s living in Seoul.
Looking for a paid date]

637
00:47:05,667 --> 00:47:07,351
<i>Show me.</i>

638
00:47:10,414 --> 00:47:11,792
<i>Keep going.</i>

639
00:47:17,635 --> 00:47:19,869
<i>- Same as before?
- Ugh.</i>

640
00:47:38,334 --> 00:47:39,858
<i>So long.</i>

641
00:47:41,707 --> 00:47:46,384
I signed that open marriage agreement
because I didn't want a divorce.

642
00:47:46,384 --> 00:47:49,751
I even agreed to it to make this work...

643
00:47:49,751 --> 00:47:52,053
Even after being fooled,

644
00:47:52,053 --> 00:47:54,453
why can't I set for a divorce?

645
00:47:55,211 --> 00:47:57,792
A woman who divorced twice.

646
00:47:57,792 --> 00:48:00,400
You're afraid of that stigma.

647
00:48:04,066 --> 00:48:05,276
Yes.

648
00:48:06,292 --> 00:48:08,715
"A woman who divorced twice."

649
00:48:08,715 --> 00:48:10,985
I'm so scared of that title.

650
00:48:13,055 --> 00:48:17,567
Attorney, what are our chances of winning?

651
00:48:18,500 --> 00:48:20,813
As of now, it's fifty-fifty.

652
00:48:20,813 --> 00:48:22,467
Fifty-fifty?

653
00:48:23,231 --> 00:48:25,125
I thought...

654
00:48:25,125 --> 00:48:27,292
you were certain.

655
00:48:27,292 --> 00:48:29,192
I'm not certain.

656
00:48:29,834 --> 00:48:33,692
But a lawyer's job is to argue
as if they are certain.

657
00:48:34,428 --> 00:48:39,516
No judge in the world rules for someone
who lacks confidence in their own words.

658
00:48:46,522 --> 00:48:49,699
[CHUNJEONG: Fighting for clients
with trust and responsibility]

659
00:48:49,699 --> 00:48:53,663
[All legal consultations are paid]

660
00:48:53,663 --> 00:48:55,863
[Corporate & Administrative Law]
[Damages]

661
00:48:55,863 --> 00:48:58,389
Man, I'm exhausted.

662
00:48:59,202 --> 00:49:00,564
[Boss]

663
00:49:09,613 --> 00:49:13,190
<i>♪ I promised to go to Seoul one day ♪</i>

664
00:49:13,190 --> 00:49:16,349
<i>♪ and become successful ♪</i>

665
00:49:16,349 --> 00:49:20,118
<i>♪ and come back ♪</i>

666
00:49:20,118 --> 00:49:26,487
<i>♪ But I got so busy crying and laughing ♪</i>

667
00:49:26,487 --> 00:49:29,584
<i>♪ that I can only go there in my dreams ♪</i>

668
00:49:29,584 --> 00:49:32,566
Councilor, I thought Attorney Kang

669
00:49:32,566 --> 00:49:36,751
was only good at her job,
but her singing is incredible too.

670
00:49:36,751 --> 00:49:38,834
Wow, Attorney Kang.

671
00:49:38,834 --> 00:49:44,483
They say people live up to their looks.
You really do have talent.

672
00:49:46,570 --> 00:49:48,959
<i>♪ My life is so lacking ♪</i>

673
00:49:48,959 --> 00:49:54,161
<i>♪ I write its diary ♪</i>

674
00:49:54,161 --> 00:49:59,627
<i>♪ while looking at the Seoul moon ♪</i>

675
00:50:04,759 --> 00:50:08,159
I'm going to step out to the restroom.

676
00:50:08,876 --> 00:50:10,850
Sure, go ahead.

677
00:50:15,417 --> 00:50:18,375
It must have been urgent.

678
00:50:18,375 --> 00:50:21,960
- I'm counting on you, Partner Kim.
- Don't you worry.

679
00:50:21,960 --> 00:50:24,533
I'll get back every cent you're owed.

680
00:50:24,533 --> 00:50:27,318
Don't worry. Who's the best at debt collection?

681
00:50:27,318 --> 00:50:28,551
Kang Hye Seong.

682
00:50:28,551 --> 00:50:31,000
- Kang Hye Seong.
- Kang Hye Seong.

683
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:32,324
It's a promise. A promise.

684
00:50:32,324 --> 00:50:34,959
- Promise.
- Promise. Don't fail me.

685
00:50:34,959 --> 00:50:37,692
Please go in. Yes, go on in.

686
00:50:39,250 --> 00:50:41,859
- Get home safe.
- I'm off.

687
00:50:45,083 --> 00:50:46,403
Sir,

688
00:50:47,608 --> 00:50:50,083
please stop making me go to these.

689
00:50:50,083 --> 00:50:54,356
And please take down that "Problem Solver"
banner hanging downtown.

690
00:50:55,709 --> 00:51:00,125
You know that could break advertising
rules under the Attorney-at-Law Act, right?

691
00:51:00,125 --> 00:51:01,565
Hey, Kang.

692
00:51:01,565 --> 00:51:04,959
Let go of trivial things!
Or you'll never be number one in Gwangjin.

693
00:51:04,959 --> 00:51:08,035
Starting tomorrow,
report to the city councilor's office.

694
00:51:09,751 --> 00:51:12,542
I have a case in Seoul tomorrow.

695
00:51:12,542 --> 00:51:16,584
You haven't finished that yet?
I told you, it's not cost-effective!

696
00:51:16,584 --> 00:51:19,385
Are you telling me to just give up on the case?

697
00:51:19,385 --> 00:51:23,352
I told you to make concessions and settle.
Didn't I tell you?

698
00:51:23,352 --> 00:51:25,570
You're not cut out for divorce cases.

699
00:51:25,570 --> 00:51:27,434
How many times have I told you?

700
00:51:28,645 --> 00:51:30,754
What's taking so long? Damn it.

701
00:51:40,369 --> 00:51:43,012
[Open Marriage Agreement]

702
00:51:51,459 --> 00:51:55,942
<i>Divorce cases are a 1% fight, not a 99% one.</i>

703
00:51:59,709 --> 00:52:01,895
Where are you going this late?

704
00:52:03,626 --> 00:52:05,483
To find that 1%.

705
00:52:23,086 --> 00:52:24,895
[My Daughter]

706
00:52:27,160 --> 00:52:28,167
Yeah?

707
00:52:28,167 --> 00:52:31,042
<i>Can I stay at Dad's for two more days?</i>

708
00:52:31,042 --> 00:52:32,211
Why all of a sudden?

709
00:52:32,211 --> 00:52:34,941
I just want to spend more time with Ji Yoon.

710
00:52:37,102 --> 00:52:39,570
Visitation is an agreement too,

711
00:52:39,570 --> 00:52:42,242
so how about we plan
the extra night in advance?

712
00:52:42,242 --> 00:52:44,308
We promised to do homework together.

713
00:52:45,042 --> 00:52:46,667
Okay.

714
00:52:46,667 --> 00:52:48,580
- Don't stay up too...
<i>- Thanks, Mom.</i>

715
00:52:48,580 --> 00:52:50,125
Hello?

716
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:52,641
- What did she say?
- She said yes.

717
00:52:56,167 --> 00:52:58,363
Oh, boy.

718
00:53:03,366 --> 00:53:05,332
[Central Family Court]

719
00:53:10,078 --> 00:53:13,610
The defendant still doesn't want a divorce.

720
00:53:16,167 --> 00:53:17,567
However.

721
00:53:18,167 --> 00:53:20,155
<i>What? No way.</i>

722
00:53:20,155 --> 00:53:22,876
If the terms we have brought are accepted,

723
00:53:22,876 --> 00:53:27,318
she is willing to agree to a divorce
and settle right here.

724
00:53:30,125 --> 00:53:33,984
<i>Did she persuade someone
who didn't want a divorce?</i>

725
00:53:39,107 --> 00:53:40,299
<i>I...</i>

726
00:53:41,091 --> 00:53:43,909
<i>I really don't want a divorce.</i>

727
00:53:43,909 --> 00:53:46,127
<i>Please. You must win this case.</i>

728
00:53:47,375 --> 00:53:52,984
<i>But if you win the case, will you
really win at life as well, Park Na Yeon?</i>

729
00:53:53,959 --> 00:53:57,262
<i>You won't become a woman who divorced twice,</i>

730
00:53:57,262 --> 00:54:02,067
<i>but is the plaintiff a partner
worth keeping this much?</i>

731
00:54:03,162 --> 00:54:04,557
<i>Is he?</i>

732
00:54:25,584 --> 00:54:31,125
The condition is that we take 100%
of the condo, which is your joint property.

733
00:54:31,125 --> 00:54:35,167
We can't accept that.
That condo was gifted by Seo Ji Hoon's father.

734
00:54:35,167 --> 00:54:38,906
Then let's make it 70-30.
70 for us, 30 for you.

735
00:54:38,906 --> 00:54:40,572
Absolutely not.

736
00:54:40,572 --> 00:54:44,201
It's separate property. The marriage lasted
under ten years with no kids.

737
00:54:44,201 --> 00:54:45,996
70-30 is ridiculous.

738
00:54:49,000 --> 00:54:51,650
I said I'm fine with it.

739
00:55:03,083 --> 00:55:06,067
I'll accept the mediation proposal.

740
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:17,025
These are market price reports for the condo
from ten realtors.

741
00:55:18,365 --> 00:55:22,959
The average price is 130 million won.
70% of that is 91 million won.

742
00:55:22,959 --> 00:55:27,626
So, you just need to pay us
40 million won in cash.

743
00:55:27,626 --> 00:55:31,567
<i>She's inflating the market value
to get a bigger payout.</i>

744
00:55:32,426 --> 00:55:35,142
<i>Did she really go and get all those herself?</i>

745
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:43,918
It's not 130 million won. It's 100 million won.

746
00:55:43,918 --> 00:55:48,192
Seems you didn't check the Ministry of Land
price data or bank AI valuation.

747
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:52,991
<i>Oh, no.</i>

748
00:55:53,613 --> 00:55:54,908
<i>Wait.</i>

749
00:56:02,792 --> 00:56:05,616
That area is scheduled for reconstruction.

750
00:56:05,616 --> 00:56:08,518
The market price is clearly going to rise.

751
00:56:08,518 --> 00:56:11,216
A clear rise in the market price?

752
00:56:11,216 --> 00:56:15,042
Exactly. So 130 million won sounds good, right?

753
00:56:15,042 --> 00:56:17,946
If you're so sure, how about this?

754
00:56:17,946 --> 00:56:21,989
Take the title of the condo and give us
90 million won,

755
00:56:21,989 --> 00:56:24,626
which is 70% of 130 million won.

756
00:56:24,626 --> 00:56:26,026
What?

757
00:56:27,125 --> 00:56:32,245
No, we don't have that much cash right now...

758
00:56:32,245 --> 00:56:35,520
<i>I did my best to score an own goal.</i>

759
00:56:36,125 --> 00:56:40,534
Unfortunately,
if we can't agree on the market price,

760
00:56:40,534 --> 00:56:43,459
we'll just scrap today's mediation.

761
00:56:43,459 --> 00:56:45,292
We'll withdraw consent to divorce.

762
00:56:45,292 --> 00:56:49,234
You're so annoyingly clingy.

763
00:56:49,959 --> 00:56:52,859
Hey, take it all.

764
00:56:53,497 --> 00:56:54,985
Just give it to her, okay?

765
00:56:54,985 --> 00:56:57,349
- You're unbelievable...
- What?

766
00:57:31,210 --> 00:57:33,989
Seo Ji Hoon, were you always like this?

767
00:57:33,989 --> 00:57:36,105
Why did you step in like that?

768
00:57:36,105 --> 00:57:39,206
You were tricked by the lawyer Cha.
You lost the condo!

769
00:57:39,206 --> 00:57:42,125
Forget it. It's not even worth that much.

770
00:57:42,125 --> 00:57:45,110
I'll call it buying my freedom
with pocket change.

771
00:57:47,042 --> 00:57:50,173
It feels so good to finally
get rid of that clingy woman.

772
00:57:54,702 --> 00:57:57,211
Since you revealed your true colors,
let me ask.

773
00:57:57,211 --> 00:57:59,202
That agreement,

774
00:57:59,202 --> 00:58:03,209
did you threaten your spouse into signing it
to justify your own cheating?

775
00:58:03,209 --> 00:58:05,442
Why did you go that far?

776
00:58:06,125 --> 00:58:11,151
How can you only love one person?
That's neglecting my duties.

777
00:58:13,334 --> 00:58:18,292
Good things only have value
when they are shared with everyone.

778
00:58:18,292 --> 00:58:21,473
Free sex is beneficial to humanity.

779
00:58:21,473 --> 00:58:24,469
You should try being generous too.

780
00:58:26,006 --> 00:58:28,709
Thanks for your hard work.

781
00:58:28,709 --> 00:58:31,442
Hey babe. Yeah, it's all over.

782
00:58:39,509 --> 00:58:43,209
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

783
00:58:43,209 --> 00:58:48,417
I almost spent my life with that man because
I cared too much about what others think.

784
00:58:48,417 --> 00:58:50,947
I was just doing my job.

785
00:58:50,947 --> 00:58:55,209
I hope the reconstruction happens,
just as Attorney Kang said.

786
00:58:55,209 --> 00:58:58,567
When you live alone,
a house is your best partner.

787
00:58:59,792 --> 00:59:01,492
Well, then.

788
00:59:22,792 --> 00:59:24,212
Attorney Cha!

789
00:59:27,959 --> 00:59:29,220
Attorney.

790
00:59:30,876 --> 00:59:33,435
You did a great job, Attorney Cha.

791
00:59:33,435 --> 00:59:37,292
<i>Now she's all smiles since the case is over.</i>

792
00:59:37,292 --> 00:59:39,417
You did a great job too, Attorney Kang.

793
00:59:39,417 --> 00:59:43,525
And I'm not a newbie. I'm in my fifth year.

794
00:59:44,709 --> 00:59:46,068
Fifth year.

795
00:59:46,996 --> 00:59:48,669
Yes, well.

796
00:59:55,751 --> 00:59:57,792
Attorney Kang?

797
00:59:57,792 --> 00:59:59,370
Yes?

798
00:59:59,370 --> 01:00:03,344
Park Na Yeon.
She really didn't sleep with anyone.

799
01:00:03,344 --> 01:00:05,201
You may not believe me, but...

800
01:00:06,392 --> 01:00:08,113
I believe you.

801
01:00:08,113 --> 01:00:10,292
So you knew?

802
01:00:10,292 --> 01:00:12,001
Whether we knew or not,

803
01:00:12,001 --> 01:00:15,492
we have to do our best
to fight for our clients.

804
01:00:15,492 --> 01:00:18,044
That's our job. Is it not, Attorney Cha?

805
01:00:21,334 --> 01:00:22,507
That's right.

806
01:00:23,207 --> 01:00:25,187
Thank you for your hard work.

807
01:00:25,834 --> 01:00:27,257
You as well.

808
01:01:00,876 --> 01:01:06,442
<i>Ma'am, the lawyer you hired
won't be able to join us.</i>

809
01:01:14,920 --> 01:01:17,510
<i>Are "private life" and "sex life"
the same thing?</i>

810
01:01:17,510 --> 01:01:19,388
<i>Your Honor, the agreement never says</i>

811
01:01:19,388 --> 01:01:24,667
<i>the plaintiff threatened
or coerced her to meet other men.</i>

812
01:01:24,667 --> 01:01:27,834
<i>These are market price reports for the condo
from ten realtors.</i>

813
01:01:27,834 --> 01:01:31,116
<i>It was obvious
her client stabbed her in the back,</i>

814
01:01:31,116 --> 01:01:33,743
<i>but she kept cool so the judge wouldn't notice.</i>

815
01:01:33,743 --> 01:01:34,959
<i>Understood.</i>

816
01:01:34,959 --> 01:01:38,459
<i>I'm your attorney, so I'll trust you
and defend you until the end.</i>

817
01:01:38,459 --> 01:01:41,820
<i>We have to do our best
to fight for our clients.</i>

818
01:01:41,820 --> 01:01:46,429
She did her best for her client
and fought until the end.

819
01:01:48,584 --> 01:01:51,042
<i>I'm not a newbie. I'm in my fifth year.</i>

820
01:01:51,042 --> 01:01:54,377
<i>At least five years' experience,
serious about divorce,</i>

821
01:01:54,377 --> 01:01:56,143
<i>and good at handling cases.</i>

822
01:01:56,143 --> 01:01:58,525
She's perfect for divorce cases.

823
01:02:00,639 --> 01:02:02,302
Found you.

824
01:02:10,820 --> 01:02:11,834
Yes.

825
01:02:11,834 --> 01:02:15,703
<i>Ma'am. I heard Attorney Park Tae Su
is in his office right now.</i>

826
01:02:15,703 --> 01:02:17,103
Okay.

827
01:02:18,292 --> 01:02:20,851
Mr. Kim, please head back to the office.

828
01:02:20,851 --> 01:02:22,465
Yes, ma'am.

829
01:02:35,502 --> 01:02:36,792
[TAESU Law Firm]

830
01:03:24,806 --> 01:03:26,159
[Park Tae Su]

831
01:03:46,334 --> 01:03:48,900
Do you have anything else to say?

832
01:03:58,459 --> 01:04:00,555
Attorney Park Tae Su.

833
01:04:13,584 --> 01:04:15,158
Eun Kyung?

834
01:04:18,053 --> 01:04:19,323
Eun Kyung.

835
01:05:35,667 --> 01:05:39,792
<i>You signed with another firm. TAESU Law Firm?</i>

836
01:05:39,792 --> 01:05:41,667
<i>Good morning, Attorney Cha.</i>

837
01:05:41,667 --> 01:05:43,631
<i>Do you know Attorney Park?</i>

838
01:05:43,631 --> 01:05:46,638
<i>We went to college together.
He's such a copycat.</i>

839
01:05:46,638 --> 01:05:47,876
<i>So you remembered.</i>

840
01:05:47,876 --> 01:05:49,918
<i>I think I found one.</i>

841
01:05:49,918 --> 01:05:53,793
<i>Then how about making TAESU your next step?</i>

842
01:05:53,793 --> 01:05:58,028
<i>Attorney Park, can we meet tomorrow?</i>
